    "## 1. Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "This project develops end-to-end deep learning solutions in **TensorFlow / Keras** for three complementary tasks:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Task 1 — CIFAR-100 Subset Image Classification & Recommendation:** We classify a 50-class subset of CIFAR-100 containing only *animals* and *people* (25,000 training images and 5,000 fixed test images, 32×32 RGB). We design, train, and compare three candidate architectures: (1) compulsory **MobileNet transfer learning**, (2) a custom **VGG-style CNN** trained from scratch, and (3) a **Mini-ResNet** trained from scratch. Based strictly on validation performance, we recommend the best model and evaluate it once on the untouched test set.\n",
    "2. **Task 2 — Image Classification on a Group-Collected Dataset:** We collect and manually label our own multi-class image dataset as a group (no web images). We adapt the recommended model from Task 1 with targeted architectural and regularisation modifications, train and evaluate it on our dataset, and visualise predictions on at least 20 images.\n",
    "3. **Task 3 — Text Analysis (Sentiment Classification):** We perform binary sentiment classification on the **IMDB Movie Reviews** dataset (50,000 reviews). We implement a complete text preprocessing pipeline (HTML/punctuation cleaning, tokenisation, vocabulary construction, and sequence padding) and train a **Bidirectional LSTM** model in Keras, followed by error analysis and discussion of limitations and improvements."
   ]
  },
